  "FLINK-36873": {
    "jira_id": "FLINK-36873",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Resolved",
    "title": "Adapting batch job progress recovery to Apache Celeborn",
    "description": "I've identified several issues while attempting to enable Apache Celeborn to support Flink batch job recovery.\r\n\r\n*1. RestoreState Invocation*\r\n * The method _*{{ShuffleMaster#restoreState}}*_ should be triggered regardless of whether the Flink job requires recovery.\r\n * This method signifies that a Flink job needs to restore its state, but it is currently called only after {_}*{{ShuffleMaster#registerJob}}*{_}.\r\n\r\n * Consequently, it might not be invoked if the Flink job does not require recovery.\r\n\r\n * For Celeborn, this creates uncertainty regarding when to initialize certain components; if the initialization occurs during {*}_{{registerJob}}_{*}, it may lack essential information from the stored snapshot, whereas if it takes place during {*}_{{restoreState}}_{*}, there is a risk that it may not be invoked at all.\r\n\r\n*2. JobID Information Requirement* \r\n * Several methods in _*{{ShuffleMaster}}*_ should include _*JobID*_ information: {*}_{{ShuffleMaster#supportsBatchSnapshot}}_{*}, {_}*{{ShuffleMaster#snapshotState}}*{_}, and {_}*{{ShuffleMaster#restoreState}}*{_}.\r\n * These methods are intended for job-granularity state storage and restoration, but they currently do not incorporate JobID.\r\n * Consequently, Celeborn is unable to determine which job triggered these calls.\r\n\r\n{*}3. Cluster granularity store/restore state{*}:\r\n * Presently, _*{{ShuffleMaster}}*_ only offers job-granularity interfaces for storing and restoring state, as the _*{{NettyShuffleService}}*_ is stateless in terms of cluster granularity.\r\n * However, _*{{Celeborn#ShuffleMaster}}*_ needs to communicate with the Celeborn Master, necessitating the storage of certain cluster-level states, such as {_}*{{CelebornAppId}}*{_}.\r\n\r\n * In my opinion, the cluster-granularity store state interface can be execute after {_}*{{ShuffleMaster#start}}*{_}, and _*{{ShuffleMaster#start}}*_ adding a snapshot parameter to restore the cluster state.",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "b868c0a44f00036e62d0a37ac4f74b525ecb855c",
        "message": "[FLINK-36873][runtime] Adapting batch job progress recovery to Apache Celeborn.",
        "author": "JunRuiLee",
        "date": "2024-12-16T06:44:35Z",
        "files": [
          {
            "PARENT_PATH": "flink-runtime/src/main/java/org/apache/flink/runtime/dispatcher/Dispatcher.java",
            "CHILD_PATH": "flink-runtime/src/main/java/org/apache/flink/runtime/dispatcher/Dispatcher.java",
            "PATH_CHANGED": false,
            "LINES_ADDED": 5,
            "LINES_DELETED": 0,
            "PARENT_LOC": 1619,
            "STATUS": "M"
          },
          {
            "PARENT_PATH": "flink-runtime/src/main/java/org/apache/flink/runtime/scheduler/adaptivebatch/AdaptiveBatchSchedulerFactory.java",
            "CHILD_PATH": "flink-runtime/src/main/java/org/apache/flink/runtime/scheduler/adaptivebatch/AdaptiveBatchSchedulerFactory.java",
            "PATH_CHANGED": false,
            "LINES_ADDED": 2,
            "LINES_DELETED": 1,
            "PARENT_LOC": 413,
            "STATUS": "M"
